{{:Header/Crusades}}Crusades are unlocked after clearing [[Grasslands]] and is first accessed through the [[Portal]]. Afterwards, it can be permanently accessed any time from the top left menu.
Crusades are an extension of [[Fight]]ing, but relies entirely on skills instead of idle attacks in order to progress. [[Ascension]] and [[Rebirth]] do not reset any progress or levels from Crusades.

== Bosses ==
Every Crusade encounter consists of 4 monsters and 1 boss, all of them having a chance to drop [[Cards]] and [[Tinkering]] materials. Once a Crusade is beaten, it may be exited which automatically increases its difficulty or it may be replayed again at the same difficulty for more loot and EXP. However, the difficulty can be changed at any time on the bottom left of the screen.

There is no cost to attempt a Crusade, but it does decrease the [[Crusades#Fight Bonus|Fight Bonus]] at earning rewards from them. Fortunately, there's a Details pane displayed on every Crusade encounter difficulty, showing both the amount of HP that must be beaten and the amount of damage that must be survived. While it becomes harder to survive and healing is more limited in difficult encounters, the amount of rewards and Crusade EXP increases, making it a worthwhile tradeoff to push as far as possible. This is especially important for increasing the benefits gained by applying [[Crusades#Crusaders|Crusaders]] to idle Crusades.

As Crusade level goes up, the more types of Crusade bosses become available.

