=== Fight Bonus ===
Fight Bonus improves the card drop chance and amount of rewards obtained when a drop is looted in active Crusade encounters. Fight Bonus doesn't affect gains from idle Crusaders, nor does it decrease the chance that [[Tinkering]] materials will drop.

Every 24 hours, it starts at 100% plus the amount awarded by "+% max Fight Bonus" [[Cards]] and "+% Fight Bonus" from [[Tinkering]] equipment. This percentage decreases by 1-4% with every Crusade attempt, down to a minimum of 0%. Crusades may still be fought indefinitely, regardless of the Fight Bonus percentage. At 0%, [[Cards]] will still drop, however at a reduced rate.

For crafting material quantity, fight bonus cap at 10% minimum and 100% maximum. (not 100% sure)

For card drop, fight bonus cap at 20% minimum and 100% maximum. (not 100% sure)

== Crusaders ==
Starting with 2, every new level adds an additional Crusader that can be used to fight Crusades offline. More idle Crusaders can be applied by equipping "+X Inactive Crusader" [[Cards]] and [[Tinkering]] equipment. Applied Crusaders will remain even after bonuses are unequipped.

Each idle Crusader generates 12 victories per day (or 1 every 2 hours), which award resources and EXP from the selected boss difficulty. Applying more Crusaders additively increases the rate these rewards are obtained, and therefore award additional resources.

